# Put your Minecraft world folder in this directory — the world ROOT, the one that contains
# `level.dat` and either `region/` or `dimensions/`, not the `region/` directory itself.
#
# Nothing in here is ever committed. A world is large, often private, and never belongs in a git
# repository, so everything is ignored and only this file and .gitkeep are kept so the directory
# itself survives a clone.
*
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep
